<VI _name="lvai_replace_image_display.vi" description="Replaces ONE front panel control of a VI, found by its label, with a .ctl through {LV.Control} Replace and saves the VI in place. lvai_generate_vi and lvai_replace_controls run it for every control given a custom .ctl (a ctl attribute, controlStyle fuse - the Fuse Design System NXG controls, issue 139; Replace keeps label, type, pane slot and wiring) and for every IMAQ Image control the AIXML asked for as style Image Display: the composer writes the plain IMAQ Image refnum, and this turns it into NI Vision's Image Display - the object LabVIEW drops from the Vision palette (vi.lib\5Cvision\5CImage Display Controls.llb). Composing that plug-in object directly gave a panel LabVIEW refused to load (2026-11-17). Runs in LabVIEW's main application instance, where the VI was generated.">
